{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Moses went.</b> From the Tent of Meeting, where he dwelled, as it is stated: 'those who encamp before the Tabernacle of YHWH — Moses and Aaron and his sons.' And he went to every tribe, to inform them that he is dying, so that they would not be afraid but would strengthen their hearts through the words of Joshua. And why did he need to exert himself and go after them — he should have gathered them with the trumpets that Moses made? Rather, Rabbi Yehoshua of Sikhnin said in the name of Rabbi Levi: the trumpets that Moses made in the wilderness — once Moses inclined to die, the Holy One, blessed be He, stored them away, so that Moses would not blow them; and they come to him, to fulfill what is stated: 'and there is no authority on the day of death.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:50.459816297Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}